 ## Background
-SLS4D was introduced as a novel approach for 4D novel-view synthesis, representing the first method to use a sparse latent space representation for dynamic neural radiance fields [S1]. It builds on the principles of D-NeRF by introducing deformation fields but replaces dense voxel grids with learnable latent codes [S1]. The method was developed to address the high parameter count of previous state-of-the-art methods like V4D and TiNeuVox [S1].
+SLS4D was proposed as a novel approach for 4D novel-view synthesis, representing the 4D space in a sparse, compact and informative latent feature space [S1]. It is the first method to use latent space representation for dynamic neural radiance fields [S1]. The method demonstrates the significant potential of implicit interpolation in neural radiance fields [S1]. It was published in IEEE Transactions on Visualization and Computer Graphics in 2024 [S1].
 
